DATA SOURCES (all 8 bound through the ViewModel's StateFlow over the KMP core, P1/S8)
  useVehicle                   → VehiclesStore.vehicle(id)          (GET /vehicles/{id})                  → vehicleState (breadcrumb)
  useVehicleDrivers            → VehicleAccessRepository.vehicleDrivers(id)     (GET …/drivers)           → driversState
  useVehicleInvitations        → VehicleAccessRepository.vehicleInvitations(id) (GET …/invitations)       → invitationsState
  useRefreshVehicleDrivers     → source.refreshVehicleDrivers(id)   (POST …/drivers/refresh)              → re-collects drivers
  useRefreshVehicleInvitations → source.refreshVehicleInvitations(id)(POST …/invitations/refresh)         → re-collects invitations
  useRemoveVehicleDriver       → source.removeVehicleDriver(id,uid) (DELETE …/drivers)                    → re-collects drivers
  useCreateVehicleInvitation   → source.createVehicleInvitation(id) (POST …/invitations)                  → re-collects invitations
  useRevokeVehicleInvitation   → source.revokeVehicleInvitation(id,iid)(POST …/invitations/{iid}/revoke)  → re-collects invitations

DECISIONS / NOTES
  - DI seam: the Android DataContainer wires no VehicleAccessStore, so — exactly as the TripDetail/DrivesList
    precedents do for TripsRepository — the host constructs a page-local HttpVehicleAccessRepository over the SAME
    resilient client + offline cache (container.api / container.cacheStore), preserving the ADR-013 freshness
    contract. The vehicle read uses the already-wired shared S8 VehiclesStore. The ViewModel's per-feed triggers
    reproduce the S8 VehicleAccessStore's exact "refresh only the affected feed on a successful mutation; refresh
    nothing on failure" semantics, so no store behaviour is lost.
  - Loading parity: the web page renders PageContainer loading={driversLoading || invitationsLoading} (the spinner
    on a first load with nothing cached for either feed); each panel then shows its DataTable (length>0) or its
    EmptyState. The port matches this exactly: page-level loading via pageIsLoading; per-panel empty/success. A
    feed that hard-errors with no cache degrades to data ?? [] → the panel's EmptyState (never a blank region);
    a feed that errors with cache stays visible + flagged stale (UiState offline), mirroring the web's graceful
    no-blank behaviour.
  - SI boundary (P1/S5): no field on this surface is unit-bearing (ids, emails, roles, urls, statuses, ISO
    stamps); the only display fold is the timestamp localisation. No SI value is stored or computed.
  - detekt: :android:detekt is NOT a green gate in this repo (it reports 344 pre-existing weighted issues across
    the module, incl. ReturnCount in the already-covered TripDetailPageModel). The four files this surface adds
    contribute ZERO new detekt findings (verified: a filtered re-run shows no com\teslasync\vehicles\VehicleAccess
    entries; the two transient ReturnCount findings were refactored away and the Model's MatchingDeclarationName
    false-positive is suppressed per the sibling *PageModel convention).

